    "turn_text": "governors and talking about the virus and what they were recommending and what the government is recommending. And I just kept thinking, but I don't have the authority as governor to tell people they can't stay home or that they have to stay home. I don't have the authority to tell them they have to close their business. That's not you know, a power granted to me. So that was what was strange and shocked me is I saw all the, and I would have candid conversations with people in government and other governors and they knew they didn't have the authority and they did it anyways. So I think that's what most people don't know is the heated conversations behind the scenes that went on, that these decisions were made knowing that that was not their job.",
