    "turn_idx": 202,
    "turn_text": "You know, there's something to be said for everybody. And I hope everybody evaluates this in their life. I know Larry and his family believe this too is that. you know, people make sacrifices to be in different positions or jobs. But and so if you're going to make those sacrifices, then live a life of significance. Then it should matter. You do things that matter. And and I was raised by parents that believed that and not to complain about stuff, but to be somebody who fixes stuff and And so it's my second nature, I think, because of the way I was raised and maybe my personality, but this world wouldn't be so broken if we had more people who decided they would just step up and solve a problem rather than just sit back and belly ache about it.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
