    "turn_idx": 204,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I think Not enough time. I'm surprised by the amount of stuff I wanted to get done that there's a lot of bureaucracy in state government that I think people don't realize. I will say and make a decision in something and there's 12,000 to 13,000 state employees out there that are used to doing something a certain way that don't want to change. They know they can outlast you if they don't want to see that kind of change. So I feel like I can't even imagine what it's like at the federal level, but there's not enough time when I first got elected. I didn't I had met Jeb Bush a couple of times. He's very. Interested in education, but he he mailed me in the mail a clock That sits on my desk that counts down the amount of time I have an office So every day I look at that clock and I see how much time I have left",
